  "title": "Ramadan & iftar",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "During **রমজান** (Ramadan) most Bangladeshi Muslims **রোজা রাখেন** — 'keep the fast' — from dawn to sunset. The verb is **রাখা** 'keep', which you met in the bazaar (**কম রাখেন**!).\n\nThe day is framed by two meals: **সেহরি** before dawn and **ইফতার** at sunset. A classic Dhaka iftar: **খেজুর** (dates), ছোলা (chickpeas), পেঁয়াজু (onion fritters), বেগুনি (aubergine fritters) and জিলাপি.\n\nInviting someone **ইফতারে** ('to iftar') is a big gesture of friendship — non-Muslim friends are warmly welcome.\n\nNote **আপনি কি রোজা রাখেন?** is polite but personal; it's fine between friends.",
